e to guard e3. [%csl Re3] } 14. Qc1 Rd8 15. Nc3 { Better for you, but his queen now guards the pawn on e3. [%csl Re3] }) 14. dxe4 { He takes your pawn, the choice of most players. Knight to c3 was his best. Against his d pawn push or queen to d2, your queen grabs his b pawn. Keep going. } 14... Nxe3 { Your knight takes the pawn and hits his queen. Now watch. [%tail] } (14... Qxb2 { The queen grabs a pawn, but his queen jumps to d4 and your attack fades. } 15. Qd4 Qxd4 16. exd4 { About level: the queens are off, and his king is safe. [%csl Rd4] }) (14... Qb4+ { The check just drives his king to f2, where it is safe. } 15. Kf2 Nf6 16. Qd4 { About level: his king and queen hold everything together. [%csl Rf2] }) 15. Qc1 Nxg2+ 16. Kf1 Ne3+ 17. Ke1 O-O { Castled, with material level again: you won back both pawns. His king went for a walk and can never castle, and your knight sits on e3 in the middle of his camp. } 0-1


